#: replaces named no turn, stood in the session for good, and the model was
#: free to resolve "the caller's last request" to any older unanswered note —
#: which is how a stale «قطع» came to be "answered" after an English question.
#: There is deliberately no "if you already replied, say nothing": the relay
#: accepts a reask only when no output epoch reached the phone for that turn,
#: and a reply the model believes it gave but the caller never heard (dropped
#: inside an interrupt fence) is exactly the case this recovers.
