#: consumed, runs for or is owed to the turn — so the relay KNOWS no work was
#: ever started for it.  The old "Don't redo any action or start new work"
#: forbade exactly the work a promise-only answer ("Sure, let me check the
#: library hours for you.", text-only, no receipt, no delegation) still owed,
#: and the request was silently lost.  It forbids REDOING what was done, and
#: says that an answer that was only a promise (or did not answer the words)
